      "scope": [
        "871 states reachable from canonical actor roots and the original explicit brain-explosion entry yield 53 action identifiers, including NULL. Original info.c action names are checksum-verified against generated metadata.",
        "The route probe replaces component entry points with boundary recorders. It verifies helper selection, arguments, world ownership, episode/commercial/map fields, original refire probabilities and projectile types; it does not independently re-prove the component implementations.",
        "Each action runs in two independent worlds with five persistent clock values. The existing per-component original-C and actual-world fixtures remain the behavior evidence."
      ]
    },
    "integration": {
      "cases": 50,
      "native": "qemu-e82zppqs",
      "hemu": true,
      "sourceSha256": "b742872abdd6b82cae09673bfa859d943bd330918e6d748cc4a622ed371a989e",
      "scope": [
        "Bind/unbind and repeated binding preserve ownership; existing callbacks, duplicate context, invalid clocks/maps and busy worlds are rejected without leaked allocations",
        "A bound world rejects deletion; missing/foreign contexts and corrupted unbind ownership throw rather than free the wrong owner",
        "Weapon-only action IDs and invalid actor IDs reject; inactive actors do not perform actions",
        "A real pain sound callback enters another world and falls its actor, preserving the first world",
        "Tracer trails read each live persistent clock pointer, independently of the world tic; episode/commercial player sounds and pending exits stay in the correct world",
        "A cube launches, flies and arrives through the actual installed dispatcher and shared thinker clock",
        "All fresh-task lifecycle cases return their heap to baseline"
      ]
    },
